                        "email": "gkeishin@gmail.com",
                        "username": "gkeishin"
                    },
                    "message": "Although Robot Framework variables are case-insensitive, it is recommended to use capital letters with non-local variable names.\n\n*** Variables ***\n${SUITE}         this value is overridden\n\nRefer https://robotframework.org/robotframework/latest/RobotFrameworkUserGuide.html#creating-variables\n\nWe will need to start enforcing in our other code as we go."
                },
                {
                    "file": "xcat/test_xcat_group.robot",
                    "line": 16,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Sridevi Ramesh",
                        "email": "sridevra@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SrideviRamesh"
                    },
                    "message": "Yes.. earlier we had a practice to have variable defined in CAPS but slowly people created in lower cases.. However I always preferred uppercase and follow the same in my code.."
                }
